From 0d428517779835eecb00879dcce3c16f1b959f0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 18:40:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] inline: substitute ParamRefs in return-phi; remove
 unsound add_signext peephole
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two independent miscompiles found via the expat 2.7.3 test suite:

1. INLINER (return-value phi staleness): phi_incoming for the merge
   block is collected from the callee's Return terminators BEFORE
   ParamRef substitution runs — and those Returns are rewritten to
   Branch(merge) so the later substitution loop never sees them. A
   callee that returns its own parameter (expat checkCharRefNumber
   after copy-prop: 'return result' where result IS the ParamRef
   value) left a stale, never-defined value id in the merge phi.
   Codegen gave it a zeroed slot: every XML char ref (&#60; &#34; ...)
   decoded to 0 -> 'not well-formed' on valid documents. Fix: apply
   paramref_subst to phi_incoming operands as well.

2. PEEPHOLE fuse_add_sign_extend, REMOVED as unsound by design: it
   rewrote 'addl %X,%X; movslq %X,%DST' into 'addl %X,%DSTd'. Its own
   SAFETY comment required 'DST was initialized with the same value'
   but nothing checked that — %DSTd is typically garbage at that point
   — and the rewrite also DROPS the sign extension entirely. In expat's
   reportProcessingInstruction the PI-target length became garbage and
   XmlNameLength walked off the end of the heap buffer (SIGSEGV in
   runtests + runtests_cxx). A sound version would still need the init
   proof AND a following sext, saving nothing: deleted, not gated.

PROOF: expat 2.7.3 configure CC=lccc CFLAGS=-O2 && make check:
was FAIL 2/2 (acc_tests ERROR + SIGSEGV) -> now PASS 2/2.
Minimal repro locked in below as regression tests.
